 this is the primary objective\n2. **Remote Code Execution via MSHTA**: Execution of remote script via signed binary proxy\n3. **Anti-forensics**: Event log clearing"},{"t":11.99,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"set_model_response","result":{"assessment":"The wardog user executed mshta.exe to fetch and run a remote script from GitHub, which then spawned multiple processes that accessed the LSA registry key and certificate stores, likely for credential enumeration or security policy reconnaissance. The System event log was cleared to remove evidence of the activity.","hypotheses":[{"behavior":"mshta.exe and spawned processes (calc.exe, Calculator.exe, RuntimeBroker.exe) accessed the LSA registry key to enumerate security configuration and potentially extract credential-related settings.","event_ids":["E008","E009","E027","E028","E036","E037"],"keywords":["LSA registry","credential enumeration","security policy","HKLM\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa","registry access","reconnaissance"]},{"behavior":"wardog executed mshta.exe with JavaScript to fetch and execute a remote SCT script from raw.githubusercontent.com, using a signed binary proxy execution technique.","event_ids":["E004","E005","E018","E045"],"keywords":["mshta","signed binary proxy execution","T1218.005","remote script execution","GetObject","JavaScript"]},{"behavior":"System event log was cleared to remove evidence of the adversary activity.","event_ids":["E002"],"keywords":["event log clearing","anti-forensics","evidence removal","System channel"]}]}},{"t":11.99,"agent":"hunter","kind":"output","output":{"assessment":"The wardog user executed mshta.exe to fetch and run a remote script from GitHub, which then spawned multiple processes that accessed the LSA registry key and certificate stores, likely for credential enumeration or security policy reconnaissance. The System event log was cleared to remove evidence of the activity.","hypotheses":[{"behavior":"mshta.exe and spawned processes 